setInterval can introduce inconsistencies in 
frame timing, leading to frame drops and uneven 
rendering, especially in situations where the 
frame calculation or rendering takes longer than
expected.

requestAnimationFrame is specifically designed for
animations. It synchronizes with the display's
refresh rate, allowing the browser to optimize 
the rendering, reducing lag and improving 
performance consistency.

By using requestAnimationFrame, the game loop synchronizes 
with the browser's refresh rate, which helps create smooth 
animations and efficient performance. This approach is better
than using setInterval because it allows the browser to 
optimize the timing of updates, especially when the tab is 
not active or the device is struggling to keep up with the 
frame rate.


